From e16382a94054d6d72bc97ffc6c0ec15688758c3b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 09:11:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] hub admission: pool-aware dispatch and pickup
 budgets (no normal claim attempts at regular 7/7)

Review t_01a1ced6e9e69510 F1/F2: with priority_slots on, the combined
regular+priority budget sent every normal ready/review row through the
CPU advisory, Board claim gate and admission.lock census, all refused
hub_capacity_full, every tick; worker pickup imported unstartable normal
foreign cards; at_capacity was lost.

- kanban_admission_pools.PoolBudget: per-tick regular/priority budget.
  Normal rows only fit regular slots; marked rows charge priority first.
- dispatch: skip rows the budget does not admit before any claim; the
  review reservation only counts admissible reviews; spawns charge pools.
- at regular 7/7: at_capacity names the regular pool and the marked-only
  priority pool; queue_note says 'regular pool full (7/7)'.
- worker pickup gets the pool budget capped to the tick total.
- N1: explicit admission_class=normal carries as absent (no probe).
- _error_fingerprint moved to kanban_db_values (FILE_LINES offset).

Workers (pools off) keep the scalar budget unchanged.
